{"version":"1","id":"hanselman","handle":"hanselman","name":"Scott Hanselman","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/e2763104a3c54967a617a207fd5f87ff","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-1.1772,"y":1.6589,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":33,"newest_post_at":"2026-02-18T18:32:17.290Z","oldest_post_at":"2021-09-20T19:37:33.259Z","features":{"hype_score":0.0,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.030303,"avg_read_time":3.0625,"summary_length_avg":311.870968,"title_length_avg":75.666667,"title_length_var":1379.131313,"tag_entropy":3.518832,"tag_diversity":1.212121,"top_tag_share":0.151515,"avg_upvotes":2.242424,"median_upvotes":1.0,"avg_comments":0.060606,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.04,"zero_engagement_share":0.454545,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.143304,"non_article_ratio":0.030303,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.137931},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[0.2206,-0.8676],"cadence_depth":[-6.3676,-6.4412],"hype_variety":[-5.25,3.5147],"title_style":[3.3088,-1.7353]},"top_tags":[["microsoft",5],["aspnet",4],[".net",4],["linux",4],["azure",3],["windows",3],["general-programming",3],["ai",2]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["GitHub Copilot for CLI for PowerShell","Updating to .NET 8, updating to IHostBuilder, and running Playwright Tests within NUnit headless or headed on any OS","Why one shot AI coding demos are misleading"],"outlier":["Gergely was paying $100/month to embed testimonials. Got annoyed. Told the agent to replace it. 20 minutes later, no third party, build passing, in production. https://t.co/M2dEk7z0aD https://t.co/x95cULtQyl"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"tqprWw1DJ","title":"Gergely was paying $100/month to embed testimonials. Got annoyed. Told the agent to replace it. 20 minutes later, no third party, build passing, in production. https://t.co/M2dEk7z0aD https://t.co/x95cULtQyl","url":"https://x.com/shanselman/status/2024182955338252501","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/gergely-was-paying-100-month-to-embed-testimonials-got-annoyed-told-the-agent-to-replace-it-20-m-tqprww1dj","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--ZrL_HSsR--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2006","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-18T18:32:17.290Z"},{"id":"q7U0m8YFu","title":"Software craftsmanship survives the AI era","url":"http://feeds.hanselman.com/~/945480746/0/scotthanselman~Is-the-craft-dead","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/is-the-craft-dead--q7u0m8yfu","summary":"Software craftsmanship remains valuable despite AI-assisted development tools. While AI can accelerate development beyond typing speed limitations, complex systems still require human judgment, good taste, and design skills. The evolution from assembly to high-level languages, Stack Overflow, and now AI represents continuous tooling improvements rather than the death of the craft. Developers will continue to play crucial roles as system architects and in cleaning up AI-generated code.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/c172803f6f358de627ab64f1affc5cf5?_a=AQAEunF","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-08T22:33:00.124Z"},{"id":"OTko9hG2g","title":"Why one shot AI coding demos are misleading","url":"http://feeds.hanselman.com/~/945480803/0/scotthanselman~The-danger-of-glamourizing-one-shots","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-danger-of-glamourizing-one-shots-otko9hg2g","summary":"AI-assisted coding shouldn't be evaluated by \"one-shot\" demonstrations where a single prompt generates complete applications. These demos often rely on well-known terms like \"Minecraft\" that carry enormous semantic weight from training data, producing generic, average implementations. Real programming requires iterative refinement to transform ambiguous requirements into specific solutions. As AI becomes more prevalent, the ability to articulate precise goals, maintain system stability through changes, and apply sound software development practices becomes more critical than ever.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/c172803f6f358de627ab64f1affc5cf5?_a=AQAEunF","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-08T22:33:00.092Z"},{"id":"xw4ZnfSaZ","title":"Automatically Signing a Windows EXE with Azure Trusted Signing, dotnet sign, and GitHub Actions","url":"http://feeds.hanselman.com/~/930373259/0/scotthanselman~Automatically-Signing-a-Windows-EXE-with-Azure-Trusted-Signing-dotnet-sign-and-GitHub-Actions","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/automatically-signing-a-windows-exe-with-azure-trusted-signing-dotnet-sign-and-github-actions-xw4znfsaz","summary":"A comprehensive guide to implementing automated code signing for Windows executables using Azure Trusted Signing service. Covers the complete setup process including Azure account configuration, identity validation, certificate profile creation, local signing with the dotnet sign tool, and CI/CD integration with GitHub Actions. Includes detailed troubleshooting for common issues like authentication failures, permission errors, and endpoint configuration problems. The guide demonstrates both manual local signing and automated pipeline signing using service principals.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/5d6115d1d1e188d2dbd0ac21584b63a6?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-11-29T00:22:59.177Z"},{"id":"Qr2lPRpYS","title":"Webcam randomly pausing in OBS, Discord, and websites - LSVCam and TikTok Studio","url":"http://feeds.hanselman.com/~/905963465/0/scotthanselman~Webcam-randomly-pausing-in-OBS-Discord-and-websites-LSVCam-and-TikTok-Studio","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/webcam-randomly-pausing-in-obs-discord-and-websites---lsvcam-and-tiktok-studio-qr2lprpys","summary":"The author describes a perplexing issue where their webcam starts pausing randomly in OBS, Discord, and web-based apps like Zencastr and Riverside. After exploring potential causes, the issue is traced to a virtual camera called LSVCam, installed by TikTok Live Studio, causing enumeration problems. The solution involves manually removing an LSVCam registry key, though it reappears when TikTok Studio is reopened.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d8d97ae2128128e007d1b46968d36f6d?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-10-09T19:32:28.000Z"},{"id":"x6sE4TQrs","title":"Open Sourcing DOS 4","url":"http://feeds.hanselman.com/~/882544025/0/scotthanselman~Open-Sourcing-DOS","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/open-sourcing-dos-4-x6se4tqrs","summary":"Microsoft, in partnership with IBM, has released the source code to MS-DOS 4.00 after ten years. It holds an important place in history as an operating system written entirely in 8086 assembly code. The release includes unreleased beta binaries and documentation, providing fascinating insights into the history of DOS.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/8bf14f6e161d8a994ba57eb5a860e976?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-04-25T16:46:13.000Z"},{"id":"eEPUbN2gP","title":"Updating to .NET 8, updating to IHostBuilder, and running Playwright Tests within NUnit headless or headed on any OS","url":"http://feeds.hanselman.com/~/873234002/0/scotthanselman~Updating-to-NET-updating-to-IHostBuilder-and-running-Playwright-Tests-within-NUnit-headless-or-headed-on-any-OS","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/updating-to-net-8-updating-to-ihostbuilder-and-running-playwright-tests-within-nunit-headless-or--eepubn2gp","summary":"Learn how to update to .NET 8, switch to using IHostBuilder, and run Playwright tests in NUnit in both headless and headed modes on any operating system.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/cadfc482c9d5e2d731cc4f5371707c82?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":18,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-03-07T01:12:13.000Z"},{"id":"tebcMDqvD","title":"Using WSL and Let's Encrypt to create Azure App Service SSL Wildcard Certificates","url":"http://feeds.hanselman.com/~/749206136/0/scotthanselman~Using-WSL-and-Lets-Encrypt-to-create-Azure-App-Service-SSL-Wildcard-Certificates","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/using-wsl-and-let-s-encrypt-to-create-azure-app-service-ssl-wildcard-certificates-tebcmdqvd","summary":"Using WSL and Let's Encrypt to create Azure App Service SSL Wildcard Certificates - Scott Hanselman's Blog. The certificates must meet the following requirements: - Exported as a password-protected PFX file, encrypted using triple DES. Contains all intermediate certificates and the root certificate in the certificate chain.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/c1f711fec044d364913d0afa22375975?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-06-27T17:17:25.000Z"},{"id":"Qm8j1cwu7","title":"GitHub Copilot for CLI for PowerShell","url":"http://feeds.hanselman.com/~/737271731/0/scotthanselman~GitHub-Copilot-for-CLI-for-PowerShell","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/github-copilot-for-cli-for-powershell-qm8j1cwu7","summary":"You can sign up for their waitlist at the Copilot for CLI site. Scott Hanselman is a former professor, former Chief Architect in finance, now speaker, consultant, father, diabetic, and author. He is a failed stand-up comic, a cornrower, and a book author.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/466ac90b486b8bb5c935b2643148271e","num_upvotes":23,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-04-25T19:48:31.793Z"},{"id":"eTIVuS9kt","title":"Use your own user @ domain for Mastodon discoverability with the WebFinger Protocol without hosting a server","url":"http://feeds.hanselman.com/~/722495722/0/scotthanselman~Use-your-own-user-domain-for-Mastodon-discoverability-with-the-WebFinger-Protocol-without-hosting-a-server","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/use-your-own-user-domain-for-mastodon-discoverability-with-the-webfinger-protocol-without-hosting--etivus9kt","summary":"Use your own user @ domain for Mastodon discoverability with the WebFinger Protocol without hosting a server. Use the URL of your own Mastodon server's webfinger response and SAVE IT as a static json file and copy it to your own server. If you want to get started with Mastodon, start here.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7332f783aef07a252693b647f91e7b55","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-12-19T07:56:40.369Z"}],"similar_handles":["huggingface","sebastianraschka","readme","tds","elixirstatus"],"opposite_handles":["webdevcody","javascriptmastery","telusko","sphaerophoria","dotnet"],"similar":[{"id":"huggingface","handle":"huggingface","name":"Hugging Face","is_squad":false,"x":-1.4877,"y":2.0196,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":360,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/f1f55c67d81a4330acf5b90b26b0c8e1","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":1.73676,"median_upvotes":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.022222,"avg_read_time":8.865922,"tag_diversity":0.447222},"top_tags_preview":[["machine-learning",190],["ai",110],["huggingface",78]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[5.2794,-3.7647],"cadence_depth":[7.3824,5.3676],"hype_variety":[5.3676,6.0294],"title_style":[-1.5441,0.0882]}},{"id":"sebastianraschka","handle":"sebastianraschka","name":"Sebastian Raschka","is_squad":false,"x":-1.7471,"y":1.8094,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":65,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/eb22d2e73d074c5598d31588ad16a51c","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.334533,"median_upvotes":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.0,"avg_read_time":15.31746,"tag_diversity":0.769231},"top_tags_preview":[["machine-learning",36],["llm",35],["deep-learning",21]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[8.4706,-4.